---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="Profile - Shri Manoj Sinha (Hon'ble Lieutenant Governor)" 
  description="Official profile of Shri Manoj Sinha, the Hon'ble Lieutenant Governor of the Union Territory of Jammu and Kashmir."
>
  <div class="space-y-0 max-w-5xl mx-auto">
    <!-- Premium Page Header Band -->
    <div class="page-header-band animate-fadeInUp">
      <nav class="breadcrumb-trail" aria-label="Breadcrumbs">
        <a href="/">Home</a>
        <span class="separator">/</span>
        <span>Key Dignitaries</span>
        <span class="separator">/</span>
        <span class="current">Shri Manoj Sinha</span>
      </nav>
      <h1>Official Profile</h1>
      <p class="page-subtitle">Jammu &amp; Kashmir State Power Development Corporation Limited (JKSPDCL)</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Main Container -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-8 animate-fadeInUp delay-200">
      
      <!-- Left Column: Portrait Card & Stats -->
      <div class="space-y-6">
        <div class="bg-white rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-6 shadow-xs text-center">
          <div class="w-36 h-36 rounded-full overflow-hidden bg-white mx-auto border-2 border-slate-200 shadow-xs relative">
            <img 
              src="/dignitaries/manoj_sinha.png" 
              alt="Shri Manoj Sinha" 
              width="144" 
              height="144" 
              class="w-full h-full object-cover object-top"
            />
          </div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-extrabold text-[#0B4F9C] mt-4 text-balance">Shri Manoj Sinha</h2>
          <div class="mt-2">
            <span class="inline-block text-[10px] text-[#0B4F9C] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider bg-slate-100 px-2.5 py-1 rounded border border-slate-200">
              Lieutenant Governor
            </span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-[10px] text-slate-500 font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest mt-2">UT of Jammu and Kashmir</p>
          
          <div class="w-12 h-0.5 bg-[#D8681B] mx-auto mt-4 rounded-full"></div>
          
          <div class="mt-4 text-left text-xs space-y-2.5 bg-slate-50 p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 text-slate-700">
            <div class="flex justify-between">
              <span class="text-slate-500 font-semibold">Assumed Office</span>
              <span class="font-bold text-slate-800">August 07, 2020</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex justify-between">
              <span class="text-slate-500 font-semibold">Education</span>
              <span class="font-bold text-slate-800 text-right">M.Tech (Civil Eng.), IIT(BHU)</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex justify-between">
              <span class="text-slate-500 font-semibold">Secretariat</span>
              <span class="font-bold text-slate-800">Lok Bhavan, J&K</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Right Column: Biography & Career details -->
      <div class="lg:col-span-2 space-y-6">
        <div class="bg-white rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-6 md:p-8 shadow-xs space-y-6">
          
          <!-- Heading Section -->
          <div>
            <h1 class="text-2xl font-extrabold text-[#0B4F9C] text-balance">Official Profile</h1>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">Detailed administrative background and biographical summary of the Lieutenant Governor.</p>
          </div>

          <!-- Section 1: Biography -->
          <section class="space-y-3">
            <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-[#0B4F9C] uppercase tracking-wider border-b border-slate-100 pb-1.5">Biography</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed text-pretty">
              Shri Manoj Sinha assumed office as the second Lieutenant Governor of the Union Territory of Jammu and Kashmir on August 7, 2020. A seasoned administrator and statesman, Shri Sinha has dedicated over four decades to public service and governance in India.
            </p>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed text-pretty">
              He was born on July 1, 1959, in Ghazipur, Uttar Pradesh. A trained Civil Engineer, Shri Sinha completed both his Bachelor of Technology (B.Tech) and Master of Technology (M.Tech) in Civil Engineering from the prestigious Institute of Technology, Banaras Hindu University (IIT-BHU). His academic background in engineering has strongly influenced his focus on infrastructure development and structured administrative reform.
            </p>
          </section>

          <!-- Section 2: Political & Administrative Career -->
          <section class="space-y-3">
            <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-[#0B4F9C] uppercase tracking-wider border-b border-slate-100 pb-1.5">Public & Ministerial Career</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed text-pretty">
              Prior to his appointment as the Lieutenant Governor of J&K, Shri Sinha served three terms as a Member of Parliament (Lok Sabha) representing the Ghazipur constituency in Uttar Pradesh (1996, 1999, and 2014).
            </p>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed text-pretty">
              During his third term, he was appointed to the Union Council of Ministers, where he held critical portfolios:
            </p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-sm text-slate-600 space-y-1 text-pretty">
              <li><strong>Union Minister of State for Railways:</strong> Spearheaded massive railway expansion, technology upgrades, and modernization initiatives across northern and eastern India.</li>
              <li><strong>Union Minister of State (Independent Charge) for Communications:</strong> Directed reforms in telecom spectrum auctions, postal services modernization, and the rural digital connectivity drive.</li>
            </ul>
          </section>

        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
